# Bundled core-extension SOURCE ships verbatim and is compiled at runtime by
# esbuild (like user extensions); its .ts entries may contain JSX, which
# Prettier's TypeScript parser cannot parse in a .ts file. Mirrors the matching
# exclusions in apps/server/tsconfig.json and apps/server/eslint.config.js.
# (Previously covered by the now-deleted top-level `examples/` entry.)
apps/server/src/core-extensions/

# Generated API-reference artifacts — emitted verbatim by their generators:
#   docs/api/openapi.json  ← `pnpm docs:export-api` (scripts/export-openapi.ts)
#   docs/api/api/**        ← `generate:api-docs` (apps/site, fumadocs generateFiles)
# Prettier-formatting them would diverge from the generator output and make the
# docs-openapi-check CI guard (regenerate + git diff) fail on every run.
# The hand-authored docs/api/meta.json and .gitkeep are deliberately NOT ignored.
docs/api/openapi.json
docs/api/api/

# Drizzle's migration bookkeeping — written by `drizzle-kit generate`, read by
# drizzle, never by a person. The lefthook pre-commit hook regenerates and
# `git add`s these AFTER its format step, so every new migration would land an
# unformatted snapshot and red-light the formatting gate (DOR-485) on a file
# nobody wrote. Same reasoning as the generated API reference above.
packages/db/drizzle/meta/

# Visual-companion design mockups. Browser artifacts, not source: the skill that
# writes them says the design decisions get captured in the spec's markdown "so
# implementing agents can consume it without reading raw HTML mockups", and its
# guidance produces deliberately compact inline CSS that Prettier expands ~6x.
# Nobody reads these as code, and every future spec that uses the skill would
# otherwise land unformatted and red-light this gate. Reformatting the five that
# exist would have added ~2,600 lines of whitespace to the PR that added the gate.
specs/*/mockups/

# Task lists emitted by the /flow DECOMPOSE stage, which lives in the external
# marketplace plugin (ADR-0297) — so unlike the changelog populator there is no
# in-repo generator to teach. Its writer emits fully-expanded JSON that Prettier
# collapses hard (marketplace-taxonomy: 211 lines to 153), so the next
# `/flow:decompose` would land red exactly the way a new drizzle snapshot would.
# Narrow on purpose: the neighbouring specs/manifest.json is written IN-repo by
# .claude/scripts/spec-manifest-ops.ts with `JSON.stringify(m, null, 2)`, whose
# output already matches Prettier byte-for-byte, so it stays checked.
specs/*/03-tasks.json

# Generated from contributing/INDEX.md by
# `node .claude/scripts/docs-coverage-map.mjs --regen`, and read at runtime by
# the docs Stop hook and /docs:reconcile. Same test the specs/manifest.json note
# above applies, with the opposite answer: that file stays checked because its
# generator's `JSON.stringify(m, null, 2)` already matches Prettier byte-for-
# byte, whereas this generator's identical call does NOT — Prettier collapses
# the short `patterns` arrays onto one line and the raw regen output expands
# them, a ~590-line divergence. Leaving it checked meant the documented fix for
# a `--check` red (`--regen`) emitted a file that then failed `format:check`, so
# the two gates could not both be green at once. Ignoring it makes the committed
# artifact byte-reproducible from the generator, which is the property
# `--check` exists to defend.
.claude/scripts/docs-coverage-map.json

# Deliberately malformed fixture: it stands for a truncated
# claude-execution-output.json, so scripts/test-review-classifier.sh can prove the
# review-failure classifier reports "unknown" instead of crashing or guessing.
# Formatting it would destroy the only thing it tests.
scripts/fixtures/review-failure/malformed.json

# Playwright's generated HTML report. Already gitignored (apps/e2e/.gitignore),
# but Prettier walks the filesystem rather than the index, so after any local
# browser-test run the repo-wide `pnpm format:check` — the gate the typecheck
# job also runs — failed on an artifact nobody wrote and nobody can commit.
apps/e2e/playwright-report/

# Next.js's own build output and generated ambient-types file (both already
# gitignored, apps/site/.gitignore). Same class as docs/api/ above — emitted
# verbatim by `next build`/`next dev`, never hand-written — but Prettier walks
# the filesystem, not the index, so `pnpm format:check` was un-greenable on any
# machine that had ever built or dev-run the site (i.e. every developer
# machine): reproduced by building apps/site, which alone put 2000+ unformatted
# files under prettier --check's path (DOR-575).
apps/site/.next/
apps/site/next-env.d.ts
